# Normalizer-orbit data and kernel-cheap checkers

For each of the 148 subgroup-class representatives `H = reps r`, the compiled
generator (`LeanDring/P5/Certificate/Generators/Twin1/NormGen.lean`) emits, as untrusted
data re-checked here by kernel `decide`:

* `normIdxData r` — index in `allBases` of `N := N_G(H)` (identified as the
  genuine normalizer in `NormCard.lean` / `NormLink1.lean`);
* `normMats r` — one `ZMod 25` matrix per generator of `N`'s echelon basis: the
  abelianized-conjugation matrix `M_n` acting on `H`'s linear-character exponent
  vectors, `(M_n)_i = expVec_B (n⁻¹ gᵢ n)`;
* `normActPos r` — the induced permutation of the character list
  `charsAt r`: `normActPos[k][p]` is the index of `actVec (M_k) (charsAt r)[p]`;
* `normLabel r` — the orbit label (index of the orbit's canonical, min-index
  representative) of each character position;
* `normIsRep r` / `normTreeGen r` / `normTreePar r` / `normTreeDepth r` — the BFS
  spanning-tree witnesses connecting each character to its orbit representative.

The checkers here are pure `ZMod 25` matrix arithmetic and `Nat` bookkeeping — no
sift. `NormOrbits.lean` assembles the whole-range checks and the aggregate counts.

**Scope.** This file certifies the orbit partition of the character lists *under
the emitted matrices* only. That those matrices genuinely realise
`N_G(H)`-conjugation (the sift/`expVec` step) is proved in `NormLink.lean`, and
the reading "vector orbit ⟺ character-pair fusion" in `PairClass.lean`.
-/

-- machine-emitted data: silence style linters (generated long lines, file-level options)
set_option linter.style.longLine false

namespace LeanDring.P5Presentation

open Fin.NatCast

set_option maxRecDepth 100000
-- file-level maxHeartbeats: dozens of decide-heavy declarations below need it
set_option linter.style.setOption false
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000

/-- Matrix action on a character exponent vector: `(M e)_i = dotZ (row_i) e`. -/
def actVecZ (M : List (List (ZMod 25))) (e : List (ZMod 25)) : List (ZMod 25) :=
  M.map (fun row => dotZ row e)

/-- Additive order (`1`, `5` or `25`) of a character exponent vector. -/
def charOrdZ (e : List (ZMod 25)) : Nat :=
  25 / (e.foldl (fun acc z => Nat.gcd acc z.val) 25)

